{
  "_comment": "M9 rulesets, Survival and Custom Game presets (stream R). Typed in src/sim/systems/rulesets.ts and custom.ts; see docs/design/M9-spec.md. A ruleset is chosen when founding a homestead and lasts for that homestead. legacyMult: harder rules pay more Legacy when that homestead founds the next one; rulesets add together (1.3 and 1.2 make 1.5) and then multiply the site's multiplier. unlock: { cycle: n } (founding from the n-th homestead or later), { achievement: id } or { quest: id }. mods: production/consumption/storage (per resource, multipliers), incidentRate, scripIncome, doorHp, raidWeight, explorerTaint (multipliers), happiness ({ value, exceptTraits }), populationCap. flags: noRadio, endlessNight, glassSky.",
  "rulesets": [
    {
      "id": "famine",
      "name": "Famine",
      "blurb": "The crops are thin, the pantry is small and everyone is hungrier than they were. HALCY calls it 'portion awareness'.",
      "legacyMult": 1.3,
      "unlock": {
        "cycle": 1
      },
      "mods": {
        "production": {
          "food": 0.7
        },
        "consumption": {
